From 3c64178046306fd0ddf56375d1a64fcfa5da72e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zigzag maintainers <maintainers@example.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 19:17:32 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] feat(sliding-sync): hand every response body to an optional
 observer
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

zigzag patch 0002 (go-port/rustcore/SDK-PATCHES.txt in the zigzag repo).

SlidingSyncBuilder::with_raw_response_observer installs a callback that
receives every sliding sync response VERBATIM — the HTTP body bytes as the
server sent them, plus the request's and the response's `pos` — after the
SDK fully handled it and persisted the new position, still under the
position lock (so in order, and only handled responses).

The request is sent wrapped in KeepRawBody, whose IncomingResponse copies
the body before ruma parses it: same endpoint, metadata and error type.
SlidingSync::current_pos() exposes the restored position at startup.

Why: an application that folds the server's JSON itself must see what the
server said; ruma's v5 types model a subset (e.g. lists.*.ops is dropped).
